article en "Explicit Doc PageSet archive v1"
body
  cons paragraph
    cons sentence
      cons code "nepl3.doc-pages-archive"
      cons text " revision 1 defines "
      cons code "ArchivedPage"
      cons text ", with ordered fields "
      cons code "registration: nepl3.doc/1 PageRegistration"
      cons text " and "
      cons code "document: nepl3.doc-archive/1 DocumentArchive"
      cons text ", and "
      cons code "PageSetArchive"
      cons text ", with ordered fields "
      cons code "pages: List(ArchivedPage)"
      cons text " and "
      cons code "files: List(nepl3.doc/1 PageFile)"
      cons text "."
      nil
    cons " This opt-in structural transport preserves page order, registrations and file bytes."
    cons " The repository checker compares its JSON and Rust descriptors and closes dependencies."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "Encoding uses each original document's native structure and maximum guest depths."
    cons " The crate-private encoder retains those exact operation-local proofs and ordered compact guest components for a future consuming resolver."
    cons " Public transport values are data, not validation proofs."
    cons " The selected archive descriptors must be present; no legacy fallback is allowed."
    cons " The enclosing envelope is checked before return."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "Decoding validates the envelope, reconstructs each document through the explicit Doc archive decoder, and uses one codec, source-admission ledger and cumulative Budget for every page."
    cons " Conflicting source revisions across documents reject."
    cons " Local declarations cannot be supplied by a different page's admitted source."
    cons " File bytes are opaque transported data, never parsed or executed by Doc core."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "This structural API does not check registration collisions, labels or links and does not establish rendering readiness."
    cons " Empty sets have the same structural status as legacy transport; consuming resolution must apply its own nonempty rule."
    cons " No compact PageSet identity, preparation-plan route or Markdown renderer is selected by this transport alone."
    cons " Existing v1 routes, domains and descriptor identities remain unchanged."
    cons " End-to-end historical generation is a separate acceptance condition."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons sentence
      cons text "Explicit consuming identities and link resolution are defined in "
      cons link relative "30-doc-pages-archive-resolution.md" none text "archive resolution"
      cons text "."
      nil
    nil
  nil
